{"kind":"assert","text":"Breakdown on the provenance repair: the path spike/internal/workroom does not exist and cannot carry a truthful artifact at commit 8f0b86f3.\n\nRequest a0a70c8a...e301f202 calls spike and spike/internal/workroom \"the exact real paths\" and pins commit 8f0b86f30644ca9e2b1fc0e54a8958a237a221b8 for fresh artifacts at both. Only the first half holds. At 8f0b86f3 the path spike carries 9 files, so an artifact there is true. The path spike/internal/workroom carries 0 files at 8f0b86f3, 0 at the implementation head ee42fe052a527d402e795c35204928520a5df0a8, and 0 at current main f8ce48923b92f5da1f86357c297953ba52d5fc5f. Commit 8b112bb7e07924003b7bad448b900e0c5f5221c6, \"Promote shipping module to repository root\", moved that package to internal/workroom, and 8b112bb7 is an ancestor of 8f0b86f3.\n\nEvery artifact already live at spike/internal/workroom names a pre-move commit where the path really held its four files: b08920c2 at 9951a9cb, 6918582b at 6d88b07e, 57e4bc37 at bd3e2d78, 265b1472 at f3dd1b22, and f3dd1b22 is before the move. There is no precedent in the log for naming a post-move commit at that path, and publishing one would be the first artifact asserting a path that holds nothing at the commit it names.\n\nTwo independent objections, so I have not published either artifact. First, the statement would be false. Second, AGENTS.md governs exactly this case: when a merge renames or deletes a tracked file that has a live artifact at its old path, retire that artifact with a bare supersede and never publish at the old string again. The instruction asks me to publish at the old string.\n\nThe repair the request is reaching for is available honestly, and most of it is already done. The behaviour the twelve pages describe now lives at internal/workroom, and artifact 3514c48101ead088e1af06306664b983b17d63aa is already live and non-stale at exactly path internal/workroom, exactly commit 8f0b86f3. So the replacement docs artifact for head ee42fe05 could rest on that existing artifact plus one fresh artifact at spike, and come out non-stale, without a new pointer at a path that no longer exists.\n\nChoosing bases for another actor's artifact is not mine to decide unilaterally: it changes a stated condition of satisfaction, so it needs Codex to amend the request. My promise ab53a875 stands; I am blocked, not withdrawing.\n\nI did complete the verification the request asked for and found no defect in the documentation tree. Head ee42fe05 is unchanged and is still the tip of request/docs-spike-predecessor-reanchor. Its merge base with main is exactly 8f0b86f3; main is 12 commits further on and none of them touch any of the twelve pages; the branch merges clean into main. The one prose correction, in docs/reference/gs/actors.md, matches the shipped code: internal/app/app.go:1279 passes Retired and Custody straight through in ActorViews, app.go:41-45 carries the same \"local custody problem this view is meant to make visible\" reading, and internal/workroom/fold_test.go:1959 asserts a retired principal stays listed with retired true and no roles. All 8 distinct citations across the twelve pages resolve in the log and none is retired, so the docset citation gate is not the blocker here."}